-- title:
--   Shifting the constant a₀ by c^N in a Drinfeld chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $q$, a commutative ring $W$, an element $c \in W$, and power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]] =$ `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W` with $v$ a unit, and write $J = (X_0, X_1)$ for the ideal generated by the two variables. Assume $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in J^{q+2}$, where $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ is `drinfeldForm q W`. Let $s$ be an element of the quotient $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(c)\cdot v - f\cdot u)$ by the principal ideal generated by $C(c)v - fu$, where $C$ denotes the constant-coefficient inclusion $W \to W[[X_0,X_1]]$. Let $a_0, a, w \in W$ and $N \in \mathbb{N}$ with $a_0 - a = c^N w$, let $e_0 \in \mathbb{N}$ satisfy $e_0 + 1 \le N(q+1)$, and let $h \in J^{e_0}$ be such that $s - \overline{C(a_0)} = \bar h$ in the quotient. Then there exists $h' \in J^{e_0}$ with $s - \overline{C(a)} = \overline{h'}$ whose coefficients agree with those of $h$ on all monomials $X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i}$ of total degree exactly $e_0$, that is, for every $i \le e_0$ the coefficient at $\mathrm{single}(0,i) + \mathrm{single}(1, e_0 - i)$ of $h'$ equals that of $h$.
--
--   This is the bookkeeping step which allows the constant term of a "pure germ" in a local Drinfeld chart $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(c)v - fu)$ to be moved inside the coset $a_0 + c^N W$ without disturbing the leading form of total degree $e_0$; in particular the leading form may be required to be nonvanishing in the $\mathbb{F}_q$-rational directions before and after the shift. It is used in the identification of the adic completions of the stalks of the Drinfeld chart at supersingular points, in the two auxiliary level structures `ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne` and `ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart_exists_sub_C_eq_mk_of_sub_eq_pow_mul.lean

import Mathlib
